TL;DR dwarf min*rs meet vampire survivors

Wot I liked
- Excellent pacing, each run does not let you let your guard down;
- Adrenaline runs;
- There are occupation-specific weapons and cross-occupation ones;
- Five professions each with 3 subspecs;
- The game can be very grindy if you wanna be tough: masteries provide small but meaningful bonuses;
- There is even equipment to tweak your dwarf's performance;
- Dozens of weapons to blast bugs with;
- Many different bugs with their own behaviour;
- A bunch of biomes with unique interactions;
- If you are a fan of DRG (I am) you will feel right at home: familiar beards, familiar picks, familiar bugs;
- Good music and memorable quips;
- Many game modes, following the modes of the coop game;
- Many game-changing artifacts you unlock by playing.

Wot I disliked
- Very basic settings. The game would play even better if there were some shortcuts;
- I don't get why lootbugs have to be meleed;
- No midrun save - it'll kick you back to the last interlevel shop;
- No R&S hotkey!?

To sum it all up, when I first looked at the concept it looked silly. However the end result went beyond my expectations: The devs went a sang a tribute to vampire survivors staying true to their main game.
